Third-party components in ua-spike
==================================

ua-spike is Spike, the RISC-V ISA simulator
(https://github.com/riscv-software-src/riscv-isa-sim), with a patch stack
added by uarchlabs. Keep this file and the notices it lists in source and
binary distributions.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Spike
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files:    everything not listed under another heading
Origin:   https://github.com/riscv-software-src/riscv-isa-sim
License:  BSD-3-Clause, see LICENSE
          Copyright (c) 2010-2017, The Regents of the University of
          California (Regents)

Spike bundles components that keep their own licenses, in their own
directories:

- berkeley-softfloat-3/ (git submodule): Berkeley SoftFloat Release 3,
  BSD-3-Clause, see berkeley-softfloat-3/COPYING.txt. softfloat/ holds
  Spike's build glue for it.
- fdt/: libfdt, GPL-2.0-or-later OR BSD-2-Clause, per the SPDX headers in
  its files. ua-spike uses it under BSD-2-Clause.

